      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a DC circuit, a capacitor stores energy in its electric field and opposes changes in voltage, but doesn't respond to changes in current significantly. In an AC circuit, a capacitor acts as a filter, allowing AC voltage to pass while blocking DC voltage. \n\nThe formula for capacitive reactance (Xc) is Xc = 1 / (2πfC), where f is the frequency of the AC circuit and C is the capacitance. This means the reactance decreases as the capacitance or frequency increases.",
